<misterromdescription>
    <!--
      Sega Model 2 core for MiSTer FPGA - Copyright (C) 2026 alphanu1
      SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

      Zero Gunner (Export, Model 2A) (Model 2A-CRX). Derived from MAME 0.289
      model2.cpp ROM_START(zeroguna), a clone of zerogun (the parent zip
      holds the shared parts). For the Model 2A core (branch model2a,
      Model2.sv M2_2A). Study R852 (the layout), R862 (this set).

      THE 2A LAYOUT (VF2's MRA), each slot zero-padded to its size:
        0x0000000  i960 program 0-512 KB (MAME maincpu 0x000000)
        0x0080000  main_data, 16 MB
        0x1080000  textures, 8 MB (4 MB loaded)
        0x1880000  polygons, 12 MB (8 MB loaded)
        0x2480000  TGP math tables, 256 KB
        0x24C0000  68000 sound program, 512 KB
        0x2540000  SCSP samples, 8 MB (4 MB loaded)
      R862, THE EXTENSION after VF2's image (the loader's second remap puts
      it in the 2A SDRAM hole, byte 0x2600000):
        0x2D40000  i960 program 512 KB-2 MB (MAME maincpu 0x080000; 512 KB
                   loaded, the rest 0 as MAME's region)
      Image: 0x2EC0000 bytes. No copro data (ROMREGION_ERASE00).

      THE PATCH at 0x700 is MAME's init_zerogun: 0x08000004 ("b" to the next
      instruction) over "st g14,(g5)" in the boot's work-RAM clear, which
      otherwise wipes the PRCB the boot copied to 0x5000b0 and reinitialised
      the processor with. MAME's i960 (and this core's) re-reads the
      interrupt table pointer from the PRCB on every interrupt; the silicon
      evidently does not (study R862). Without the patch the first interrupt
      vectors through a zeroed table.

      THE 315-5881 (MAME's key 042c0d13, ROM_PARAMETER) is not modelled on
      this core (study R862): its decryption window at 0x01d90000 reads 0.
      The game uses the chip only as a check (study R873): eleven copies of
      one sequence decrypt 8 bytes, compare them as a double with a table
      in the program, and on a mismatch add 1 to a counter at 0x513000; the
      main loop stops the game once the counter passes 10 (the black screen
      after the first credit). THE ELEVEN PATCHES below turn each check's
      "be" past the increment into "b" (opcode 0x12 -> 0x08, the same
      displacement), so the counter stays 0 as with the chip. The code runs
      from the boot's copy of program 0x40000-0xcebff at 0x540000, so the
      patches are on the program image the copy is made from. The game's
      random number generator adds program words to its seed, so its
      sequence parts from MAME's when it lands on a patched word (as with
      the 0x700 patch); in MAME the game is otherwise identical (R873).

      Index 4, the game ID: 0x12 (R862). Bit 7 is SET in this MRA (0x92): the 15 kHz CRT flag (R795), which
      starts the core in 15 kHz interlaced whatever the OSD says (R908).
    -->
    <name>Zero Gunner (Export, Model 2A) [15kHz CRT]</name>
    <setname>zeroguna</setname>
    <rbf>Model2A</rbf>
    <!-- R945: the NVRAM file is the backup RAM (16 KB), "M2EEPROM" and the
         93C46 EEPROM (128 bytes): the game's settings. Needs a core built
         with R945 or later; an earlier core would wrap the extra bytes onto
         the start of backup RAM. -->
    <nvram index="2" size="16520"/>
    <rom index="4" md5="none">
        <part>92 00</part>
    </rom>
    <mameversion>0289</mameversion>
    <year>1997</year>
    <manufacturer>Psikyo</manufacturer>
    <category>Shooter</category>

    <rom index="0" zip="zeroguna.zip|zerogun.zip" md5="none">

        <!-- 0x0000000  i960 program 0-512 KB -->
        <interleave output="32">
            <part name="epr-20437.12" crc="fad30cc0" map="0021" offset="0x000000" length="0x040000"/>
            <part name="epr-20438.13" crc="ca364408" map="2100" offset="0x000000" length="0x040000"/>
        </interleave>

        <!-- 0x0080000  i960 data, 16 MB -->
        <interleave output="32">
            <part name="mpr-20296.10" crc="072d8a5e" map="0021"/>
            <part name="mpr-20297.11" crc="ba6a825b" map="2100"/>
        </interleave>
        <interleave output="32">
            <part name="mpr-20294.8" crc="a0bd1474" map="0021"/>
            <part name="mpr-20295.9" crc="c548cced" map="2100"/>
        </interleave>

        <!-- 0x1080000  textures, 8 MB -->
        <interleave output="32">
            <part name="mpr-20301.25" crc="52010fb2" map="0021"/>
            <part name="mpr-20300.24" crc="6f042792" map="2100"/>
        </interleave>
        <part repeat="4194304">00</part>

        <!-- 0x1880000  polygons, 12 MB -->
        <interleave output="32">
            <part name="mpr-20298.16" crc="8ab782fc" map="0021"/>
            <part name="mpr-20299.20" crc="90e20cdb" map="2100"/>
        </interleave>
        <part repeat="4194304">00</part>

        <!-- 0x2480000  TGP math tables, 256 KB -->
        <interleave output="32">
            <part name="opr-14742a.45" crc="90c6b117" map="0021"/>
            <part name="opr-14743a.46" crc="ae7f446b" map="2100"/>
        </interleave>

        <!-- 0x24C0000  68000 sound program, 512 KB (16-bit, byte-swapped) -->
        <interleave output="16">
            <part name="epr-20302.30" crc="44ff50d2" map="12"/>
        </interleave>

        <!-- 0x2540000  SCSP samples, 8 MB (16-bit, byte-swapped); moved by the
             loader to SDRAM byte 0x3400000 -->
        <interleave output="16">
            <part name="mpr-20303.31" crc="c040973f" map="12"/>
        </interleave>
        <interleave output="16">
            <part name="mpr-20304.32" crc="6decfe83" map="12"/>
        </interleave>
        <part repeat="4194304">00</part>

        <!-- 0x2D40000  i960 program 512 KB-2 MB (R862) -->
        <interleave output="32">
            <part name="epr-20437.12" crc="fad30cc0" map="0021" offset="0x040000" length="0x040000"/>
            <part name="epr-20438.13" crc="ca364408" map="2100" offset="0x040000" length="0x040000"/>
        </interleave>
        <part repeat="1048576">00</part>

        <!-- MAME init_zerogun: maincpu 0x700 = 0x08000004 (little-endian) -->
        <patch offset="0x700">04 00 00 08</patch>

        <!-- R873: the 315-5881 checks, "be" -> "b" (run from RAM 0x5xxxxx) -->
        <patch offset="0x443c8">28 00 00 08</patch>
        <patch offset="0x446e0">18 00 00 08</patch>
        <patch offset="0x449bc">18 00 00 08</patch>
        <patch offset="0x44bac">18 00 00 08</patch>
        <patch offset="0x44e14">18 00 00 08</patch>
        <patch offset="0x474dc">18 00 00 08</patch>
        <patch offset="0x475e8">18 00 00 08</patch>
        <patch offset="0x477f4">18 00 00 08</patch>
        <patch offset="0x4cc34">18 00 00 08</patch>
        <patch offset="0x55cd4">18 00 00 08</patch>
        <patch offset="0x56204">18 00 00 08</patch>

    </rom>

    <!-- Player 1 on joystick 1, player 2 on joystick 2, the same buttons. -->
    <buttons names="Button 1,Button 2,Start,Coin,Test,Service"/>
</misterromdescription>
